  |title Intelligence inhabits an axis with one-way visibility

  |quote
    I first read the Blub paradox shortly after "Hackers and Painters" was published-- around 2000. I first realized the same applies to *pain* when considering sacrifice and empathy as I pondered how the Savior could take upon Himself the pains of humanity. It was driven home when my wife, 8 months pregnant, 18 years ago, broke her ankle. She could empathize with someone who had a sprained ankle easily-- or even someone who broke theres while not pregnant-- but the other direction could only guess. And yet only in the last few months did I start even caring enough to look for other philosophy prior art and made the determination that it should almost certainly be called higher *orders* of intelligence because the moment it looks scalar or "greater intelligence" we're back to forgetting what axis intelligence really inhabits-- one with one-way visibility...

  |occasion
    Explaining, in passing, that most of the last year's work has been synthesizing
    things long settled in his thinking — and giving the twenty-five-year provenance of
    one of them.

  |about
    Two things worth having together. The claim: the Blub paradox generalizes to *pain*
    and to intelligence, so the axis is orders with one-way visibility rather than a
    scalar — and the moment it looks scalar the insight is lost. And the provenance:
    read in 2000, understood through his wife's broken ankle at eight months pregnant
    eighteen years ago, and only in recent months checked against prior art. The second
    is a specimen of how long a genuinely-held idea can precede its formalization.

  |before-acting
    - You are about to describe an intelligence difference as "greater" or "more
      capable".
    - You are reasoning about what a more capable mind would or would not be able to
      see.
    - You are assessing whether you can evaluate work above your own level.

  |on-reading
    - Joseph presents an idea as long-settled — its formalization may be new but the
      idea is not.

  |see
    - #exm-agi-not-substrate

